{"clause_id":"INST-2026-DP1","doc_id":"institute_annex_2026","doc_title":"Institute Procurement Annex 2026","doc_type":"policy","version":"2026","effective_date":"2026-01-01","section_path":"Delegation of Financial Powers > Delegation of Powers: Direct Purchase without Quotation","page":1,"text":"### [INST-2026-DP1] Delegation of Powers: Direct Purchase without Quotation\nUnder the authority of Goods Manual 2024 (Para 4.12), the Head of Department (HoD) is empowered to sanction direct purchase of goods valued up to INR 50,000 on each occasion without inviting quotations or bids, subject to budgetary allocation. Mandatory documentation: Purchase Indent (FORM-INDENT) and Sanction Order.","is_current":true,"superseded_by":null,"authority_rank":3}
{"clause_id":"INST-2026-DP2","doc_id":"institute_annex_2026","doc_title":"Institute Procurement Annex 2026","doc_type":"policy","version":"2026","effective_date":"2026-01-01","section_path":"Delegation of Financial Powers > Delegation of Powers: Purchase by Local Purchase Committee","page":1,"text":"### [INST-2026-DP2] Delegation of Powers: Purchase by Local Purchase Committee\nUnder Goods Manual 2024 (Para 4.13), the Dean (R&D / Academic) is designated as the approving authority for procurement of goods valued above INR 50,000 and up to INR 5,00,000. Procurement must be executed through a duly constituted three-member Local Purchase Committee. A minimum of three formal quotations must be obtained and evaluated via a Comparative Statement of Quotations (FORM-CSQ) and Purchase Committee Certificate (FORM-PCC).","is_current":true,"superseded_by":null,"authority_rank":3}
{"clause_id":"INST-2026-DP3","doc_id":"institute_annex_2026","doc_title":"Institute Procurement Annex 2026","doc_type":"policy","version":"2026","effective_date":"2026-01-01","section_path":"Delegation of Financial Powers > Delegation of Powers: High Value Tenders and Proprietary Single Source","page":1,"text":"### [INST-2026-DP3] Delegation of Powers: High Value Tenders and Proprietary Single Source\nProcurement of goods exceeding INR 5,00,000 shall be approved as follows:\n1. Limited Tender Enquiry (LTE) from INR 5,00,000 to INR 25,00,000: Approving authority is the Director. Minimum of 3 competitive bids required.\n2. Advertised Tender Enquiry (ATE / CPPP / GeM) exceeding INR 25,00,000: Approving authority is the Director / Board of Governors. Open public tender mandatory.\n3. Proprietary Article / Sole Source Procurement under GFR Rule 166: Irrespective of value, sole source procurements require justification and approval of the Director.","is_current":true,"superseded_by":null,"authority_rank":3}
{"clause_id":"INST-2026-DP4","doc_id":"institute_annex_2026","doc_title":"Institute Procurement Annex 2026","doc_type":"policy","version":"2026","effective_date":"2026-01-01","section_path":"Delegation of Financial Powers > Delegation of Powers: Emergency Urgency Procurement","page":1,"text":"### [INST-2026-DP4] Delegation of Powers: Emergency Urgency Procurement\nIn unforeseen operational contingencies, natural disasters, or critical lab/facility breakdown, the Head of Department (HoD) is authorized to invoke emergency procurement powers for goods valued up to INR 50,000 on each occasion without prior committee constitution. The indenting officer must table a post-facto ratification report to the Director within 48 hours of order placement.","is_current":true,"superseded_by":null,"authority_rank":3}
{"clause_id":"FORM-INDENT","doc_id":"forms_2026","doc_title":"Standard Procurement Form (FORM-INDENT)","doc_type":"form","version":"2026","effective_date":"2026-01-01","section_path":"Forms Repository > FORM-INDENT","page":1,"text":"# Institutional Purchase Indent Form\n\n**Form ID:** FORM-INDENT  \n**Ref Policy:** INST-2026-DP1 / INST-2026-DP2  \n**Date:** {{ DATE }}  \n**Department:** {{ DEPARTMENT }}  \n\n## 1. Indent Particulars\n- **Indenting Officer:** {{ INDENTER_NAME }}\n- **Item Description & Technical Specifications:** {{ ITEM_DESCRIPTION }}\n- **Quantity Required:** {{ QUANTITY }}\n- **Estimated Total Cost (INR):** {{ ESTIMATED_VALUE }}\n- **Budget Head / Project Grant Code:** {{ BUDGET_HEAD }}\n\n## 2. Procurement Justification & Category\n- Category: [ ] Goods  [ ] Services  [ ] Works\n- Mode: [ ] Direct Purchase (<= 50,000 INR)  [ ] Purchase Committee (> 50,000 INR)  [ ] Emergency\n\n## 3. Sanction Approval\n**Indenting Officer Signature:** ____________________  \n**Head of Department / Sanctioning Authority:** ____________________","is_current":true,"superseded_by":null,"authority_rank":4}
{"clause_id":"FORM-CSQ","doc_id":"forms_2026","doc_title":"Standard Procurement Form (FORM-CSQ)","doc_type":"form","version":"2026","effective_date":"2026-01-01","section_path":"Forms Repository > FORM-CSQ","page":1,"text":"# Comparative Statement of Quotations (CSQ)\n\n**Form ID:** FORM-CSQ  \n**Ref Policy:** MGP-2024-C4.13 / GFR-2017-R155 / INST-2026-DP2  \n**Requirement Reference:** {{ INDENT_REF }}  \n\n## 1. Summary of Quotations Received\n*(Statutory Minimum of 3 Responsive Quotations Required for LPC and LTE)*\n\n| Sl. No. | Vendor Name | Basic Quoted Rate | GST / Taxes | Freight & Packing | Landed Total (INR) | Delivery Period | Compliant (Y/N) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | M/s Vendor A | | | | | | |\n| 2 | M/s Vendor B | | | | | | |\n| 3 | M/s Vendor C | | | | | | |\n\n## 2. Evaluation & L1 Determination\n- **Recommended Lowest Evaluated Responsive Bidder (L1):** {{ L1_VENDOR }}\n- **Total Recommended Sanction Value:** INR {{ L1_TOTAL }}\n\n**Signatures of Committee / Evaluating Officers:**  \n1. __________________  \n2. __________________  \n3. __________________","is_current":true,"superseded_by":null,"authority_rank":4}
{"clause_id":"FORM-PCC","doc_id":"forms_2026","doc_title":"Standard Procurement Form (FORM-PCC)","doc_type":"form","version":"2026","effective_date":"2026-01-01","section_path":"Forms Repository > FORM-PCC","page":1,"text":"# Purchase Committee Certificate (PCC)\n\n**Form ID:** FORM-PCC  \n**Ref Policy:** MGP-2024-C4.13 / INST-2026-DP2  \n**Sanction Band:** INR 50,001 to INR 5,00,000  \n\n## Mandatory Statutory Certificate\n\"We, the members of the Local Purchase Committee, certify that we have jointly surveyed the market, verified the technical specifications of the quotations received, and satisfied ourselves that the recommended goods meet quality specifications, are priced fairly and reasonably at prevailing market rates, and that the recommended supplier is the lowest responsive bidder.\"\n\n## Committee Members\n1. **Chairperson (Nominee of Dean R&D/Academic):** {{ CHAIR_NAME }}  \n   Signature: ______________________ Date: ___________\n2. **Technical Member:** {{ TECH_MEMBER }}  \n   Signature: ______________________ Date: ___________\n3. **Accounts / Administrative Member:** {{ ACCOUNTS_MEMBER }}  \n   Signature: ______________________ Date: ___________\n\n**Approving Authority Approval:**  \nDean (R&D / Academic)  \nSignature: ______________________ Date: ___________","is_current":true,"superseded_by":null,"authority_rank":4}
